# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC <a id="section-1"></a>
# MAGIC ## 1. Delta tables that stay in OneLake
# MAGIC **The idea:** you don't have to move everything before you get value. Delta tables in **OneLake** can be registered in Unity Catalog through **catalog federation** as *foreign Delta tables*, governed there, and **shared through OpenSharing without copying the data**. Sharing foreign Delta tables is GA (September 2026).
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **How it works:**
# MAGIC 1. Set up catalog federation to OneLake so the tables show up as a foreign catalog (docs: *What is catalog federation?* and *Work with foreign tables*).
# MAGIC 2. Add the foreign Delta tables to a share (docs: *Create shares for OpenSharing* > *Add foreign Delta tables to a share*).
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Notes:** Databricks recipients read the source Delta files directly using cloud tokens. Pre-signed URL access doesn't support Delta tables stored in OneLake, so non-Databricks recipients may be limited. Check *Cloud token eligibility* in the docs.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC [↑ Back to contents](#contents)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Read-only: list foreign catalogs already registered in this metastore
# Read-only: list foreign catalogs already registered in this metastore.
display(spark.sql("SHOW CATALOGS"))

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC <a id="section-2"></a>
# MAGIC ## 2. An acquired company's database with Lakehouse Federation
# MAGIC **The idea:** create a **connection** to the acquired business's database and a **foreign catalog** that mirrors it in Unity Catalog. Teams can query and join that data with your own right away, under one set of permissions, and you decide later what to migrate. Since September 2026 you can also **share** foreign schemas and tables through OpenSharing without copying them.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Supported connection types in SQL:** `SQLSERVER` (SQL Server, Azure SQL Database, Azure SQL Managed Instance), `SQLDW` (Azure Synapse), `POSTGRESQL`, `MYSQL`, `REDSHIFT`, `SNOWFLAKE`, `DATABRICKS`.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Permissions:** you MUST be a metastore admin or have `CREATE CONNECTION`. Credentials SHOULD come from Databricks secrets, never plain text.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Docs: *Run federated queries on Microsoft SQL Server*, *CREATE CONNECTION*.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC [↑ Back to contents](#contents)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,CREATES A CONNECTION + FOREIGN CATALOG
# CREATES A CONNECTION + FOREIGN CATALOG. Fill in the values, store credentials in a secret scope, then set RUN = True.
RUN = False
CONN = "acq_sqlserver"
FOREIGN_CATALOG = "acq_erp"
HOST, PORT, DATABASE = "<hostname>", "1433", "<database>"
SCOPE, USER_KEY, PWD_KEY = "<secret-scope>", "<secret-key-user>", "<secret-key-password>"
sql_conn = f"""
CREATE CONNECTION IF NOT EXISTS {CONN} TYPE sqlserver
OPTIONS (
  host '{HOST}',
  port '{PORT}',
  user secret('{SCOPE}', '{USER_KEY}'),
  password secret('{SCOPE}', '{PWD_KEY}')
)"""
sql_cat = f"CREATE FOREIGN CATALOG IF NOT EXISTS {FOREIGN_CATALOG} USING CONNECTION {CONN} OPTIONS (database '{DATABASE}')"
if RUN:
    spark.sql(sql_conn); spark.sql(sql_cat); print("Created.")
else:
    print(sql_conn); print(sql_cat)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Read-only: explore the federated data once the catalog exists
# Read-only: explore the federated data once the catalog exists.
display(spark.sql(f"SHOW SCHEMAS IN {FOREIGN_CATALOG}"))

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC <a id="section-3"></a>
# MAGIC ## 3. Share governed metrics with partner or member organizations
# MAGIC **The idea:** define metrics once as **Unity Catalog metric views** and share them through OpenSharing. Recipients query them with `MEASURE(...)` on serverless compute, so every organization uses the same definition of a number without you shipping raw tables. Sharing metric views is GA (September 2026).
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Limitations to check first:**
# MAGIC * Metric views can only be shared with **Databricks recipients**. Members without Databricks need a regular table or view share instead.
# MAGIC * The metric view MUST NOT reference tables with row filters, column masks, ABAC policies, or **catalog commits** enabled. Catalog commits are now applied to tables by automatic upgrades, so check this.
# MAGIC * Only the function subset supported for shared views is allowed.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Docs: *Create shares for OpenSharing* > *Add metric views to a share*.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC [↑ Back to contents](#contents)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,CREATES A SHARE + RECIPIENT AND GRANTS ACCESS
# CREATES A SHARE + RECIPIENT AND GRANTS ACCESS. Fill in the values, then set RUN = True.
RUN = False
SHARE = "member_metrics"
METRIC_VIEW = f"{CATALOG}.{SCHEMA}.mv_member_kpis"     # your metric view
RECIPIENT = "member_company_a"
RECIPIENT_SHARING_ID = "<recipient-sharing-identifier>"   # from the member's Databricks workspace
stmts = [
  f"CREATE SHARE IF NOT EXISTS {SHARE} COMMENT 'Governed KPIs for member companies'",
  f"ALTER SHARE {SHARE} ADD VIEW {METRIC_VIEW}",          # metric views use the VIEW data type
  f"CREATE RECIPIENT IF NOT EXISTS {RECIPIENT} USING ID '{RECIPIENT_SHARING_ID}'",
  f"GRANT SELECT ON SHARE {SHARE} TO RECIPIENT {RECIPIENT}",
]
for s in stmts:
    print(s)
    if RUN: spark.sql(s)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Read-only: check what a share contains and who can read it
# Read-only: check what a share contains and who can read it.
display(spark.sql(f"SHOW ALL IN SHARE {SHARE}"))
display(spark.sql(f"SHOW GRANTS ON SHARE {SHARE}"))

# COMMAND ----------

